WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:17.300
GOES-16, formerly known as GOES-R before reaching geostationary orbit, is the first of the GOES-R series of Geostationary Operational Environmental Satellites (GOES) operated by NASA and the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA).

00:17.847 --> 00:23.938
GOES-16 serves as a backup for NOAA’s operational geostationary constellation.

00:24.558 --> 00:37.740
GOES-16 provides high spatial and temporal resolution imagery of the Earth through 16 spectral bands at visible and infrared wavelengths using its Advanced Baseline Imager (ABI).
